8)Divsors of number
Input: n = 6
Output = [1, 2, 3, 6]
Explanation: The divisors of 6 are 1, 2, 3, 6.
Brute force:
class Solution {
    public int[] divisors(int n) {
     int arr1 [] = new int[n];
     int num=0;
     for(int i=1;i<=n;i++){
        if(n%i==0){
            arr1[num]=i;
            num++;
        }    
     }
     int arr2 [] = new int[num];
     for(int j=0;j<num;j++){
        arr2[j]=arr1[j];
     }
     return arr2;
    }
}
Time Complexity: O(n), Space Complexity: O(k) (where k is the number of divisors).
